Reason: seed numpy's global generator alongside torch's. KGPFN's eval-time in-context retrieval shuffles candidate lists with np.random.shuffle (pfn/tasks.py::build_context_relation_aware), and upstream seeds only torch -- so two runs of one graph from one checkpoint sample different contexts and produce different numbers. The seed value is args.seed + rank, exactly the pattern upstream uses for torch; nothing else changes. Same defect and same fix as FLOCK (patches/flock/0004).

diff --git a/script/test_kgpfn.py b/script/test_kgpfn.py
index 3abb34f..6e24aa8 100644
--- a/script/test_kgpfn.py
+++ b/script/test_kgpfn.py
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ import contextlib
 import yaml
 from typing import Any
 
+import numpy as np
 import torch
 from torch import optim
 from torch import nn
@@ -1107,6 +1108,12 @@ if __name__ == "__main__":
         _save_configs(cfg, args.config, working_dir)
 
     torch.manual_seed(args.seed + util.get_rank())
+    # Eval-time context retrieval draws through numpy as well as torch:
+    # pfn/tasks.py::build_context_relation_aware shuffles the 2-hop
+    # candidate list with np.random.shuffle. Upstream seeds only torch,
+    # so two runs of one graph sample different contexts and score
+    # differently. Same defect and same fix as FLOCK (patches/flock/0004).
+    np.random.seed(args.seed + util.get_rank())
 
     # 日志：输出到控制台 + .log 文件（默认 pretrain_pfn.log，写入 working_dir）
     # 必须用 abspath，否则 chdir(working_dir) 后相对路径会重复解析
